Subject: [PATCH 0/3] Input: msg2638 - msg2138 fixes for the msg2133

The PocketBook 624 e-book reader (Allwinner A13) uses an MStar msg2133
touch controller, which speaks the same protocol as the msg2138 that the
msg2638 driver already supports. Bringing it up showed two driver issues
and one binding limitation:

1. The second finger is a signed 12-bit offset from the first one, but
   the driver adds it unsigned.
2. The firmware needs ~1.2 s after reset before it answers on I2C, and
   every interrupt in that window is logged as a failed transfer.
3. The binding does not allow touchscreen-inverted-x/-swapped-x-y,
   which this board needs (the panel is mounted rotated).

The board DT using this is sent separately to the sunxi maintainers.


meteowrite (3):
  Input: msg2638 - fix msg2138 second finger position
  Input: msg2638 - don't log I2C errors while the msg2138 firmware boots
  dt-bindings: input: touchscreen: msg2638: Allow common touchscreen
    properties

 .../input/touchscreen/mstar,msg2638.yaml      |  2 +-
 drivers/input/touchscreen/msg2638.c           | 19 +++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

